{
  "name": "twilight_sweep_survey",
  "saveFile": "minimal_colony.rws",
  "description": "SURVEY ONLY, no pins: locates \u00a726's sweep window on this tile before the A/B pins anything in it. Every Probe carries a dummy expectation and a huge tolerance, so the scenario passes regardless and the numbers are read out of the report's ActualValue fields. \u00a726's window runs from the horizon to \u00a78's -6\u00b0 fade floor, which is roughly three times \u00a723b's, but RimWorld's clock does not put sunset at 18:00 and the window's ENDS are what the A/B needs \u2014 the envelope is zero at both of them by construction, so an hour picked just inside one reads as a healthy non-zero position with nothing at all on screen. Latitude 45, day 40, Clear: \u00a726 reads no cloud fraction, and a cloudless sky keeps the three cloud lanes from confounding it.",
